@@@ meta
id: ARR-H-09
topic: Arrays
difficulty: Hard
type: FIND_THE_BUG
title: Median Filter That Corrupts Its Own Sample History
tags: embedded, median-filter, circular-buffer, insertion-sort, aliasing, spike-rejection
@@@ statement_md
A wheel-speed sensor occasionally produces single-sample spikes (EMI from the ignition). A **5-tap median filter** removes them: each output is the median of the last 5 samples. During the warm-up (fewer than 5 samples so far) it is the **lower median** of the samples received so far, i.e. element `(count - 1) / 2` of them in sorted order.

The window is kept in a small circular buffer `win[5]` with a write index `idx`. The first five outputs are always right. After that the filter sometimes lets a spike through or returns a value that is not in the last five samples at all, and on a constant signal with one spike it can stay wrong for several cycles.

Find and fix the bug. Do not change the input or output format.

**Input**
- Line 1: `n`. Line 2: `n` samples (`int16_t`).

**Output**
- The `n` filtered values on one line.

**Example**
```
Input:
7
10 50 20 40 30 1000 35

Output:
10 10 20 20 30 40 35
```
The 7th output is the median of `20 40 30 1000 35`, which is `35`.
@@@ constraints_md
- `1 <= n <= 100000`
- `-32768 <= sample <= 32767`
- Window length 5, lower median during warm-up.
@@@ starter_code
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <string.h>

#define WIN 5u

typedef struct {
    int16_t win[WIN];   /* circular history of the last WIN samples */
    uint8_t idx;        /* slot of the oldest sample (next to overwrite) */
    uint8_t count;      /* samples held, saturates at WIN */
} median_t;

static void sort_i16(int16_t *v, unsigned n)          /* insertion sort, n <= 5 */
{
    for (unsigned i = 1; i < n; i++) {
        int16_t key = v[i];
        unsigned j = i;
        while (j > 0 && v[j - 1] > key) {
            v[j] = v[j - 1];
            j--;
        }
        v[j] = key;
    }
}

static int16_t median_update(median_t *m, int16_t x)
{
    m->win[m->idx] = x;                               /* replace the oldest sample */
    m->idx = (uint8_t)((m->idx + 1u) % WIN);
    if (m->count < WIN)
        m->count++;

    int16_t *v = m->win;
    sort_i16(v, m->count);
    return v[(m->count - 1u) / 2u];                   /* (lower) median */
}

int main(void)
{
    int n;
    if (scanf("%d", &n) != 1 || n < 1) return 0;
    median_t filt;
    memset(&filt, 0, sizeof filt);
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        int x;
        if (scanf("%d", &x) != 1) return 0;
        printf("%d%c", median_update(&filt, (int16_t)x), i == n - 1 ? '\n' : ' ');
    }
    return 0;
}
